.SH "Constructor & Destructor Documentation"
.PP 
.SS "csmp::ErrorHandler::~ErrorHandler ()"

.PP
writes a file called 'Runtime\&.log' with all the current messages when the program terminates The destructor of the \fBErrorHandler\fP has a special role in that it dumps all the recorded messages in sequential order into the text file 'ErrorHandler\&.log' for examination of the conditions which caused a fatal error or which occurred until the normal termination of the run\&.
.SH "Application Examples"
.PP
Destructors are called automatically when a C++ program exits normally\&. If the Terminate() method ends the run it prompts the generation of the same logfile\&. 
.SH "Member Function Documentation"
.PP 
